    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling Saturday, anchored by **Junior Caminero** (80.95) and **Yordan Alvarez** (79.83), who represent our strongest offensive plays. **Junior Caminero** benefits from a high-leverage matchup against Grayson Rodriguez, whose 4.74 xERA provides an ideal environment for **Junior Caminero** to drive run production from the cleanup spot. Simultaneously, **Yordan Alvarez** continues to dominate with an elite 0.452 xwOBA, and his favorable platoon edge against Stephen Kolek suggests he is the most likely candidate to provide multi-hit value today. While **Luke Raley** (64.39) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (62.11) also grade out as strong starts, keep a close watch on **Pete Crow-Armstrong**; despite the 10% boost for hitting atop the order, his efficiency is pressured by an elite defensive catcher and a tough matchup against Logan Webb.\n\nThe tightest decision on today's board occurred at the fringes of the utility spots, where **Carson Benge** (55.18) was narrowly edged out by the superior power-projection of **Lars Nootbaar** (60.93). **Carson Benge** offered a respectable floor, but **Lars Nootbaar** secured the final OF start due to an 11% dynamic platoon advantage and a favorable matchup against Taj Bradley. We are managing significant risk at the C and OF3 positions; both **Gary Sanchez** (40.83) and **Christian Yelich** (41.24) are hovering near their respective floors, largely due to the formidable presence of Cristopher S\u00e1nchez on the mound (2.72 xERA). Their inclusion remains strategic, but their proximity to the \"below floor\" threshold means we are one early-inning pull away from pivoting to bench depth if the game-cap situation requires it. Ensure all lineups are confirmed, as our reliance on assumed batting order positions for players like **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Colt Keith** introduces volatility if they slide down in the actual card.",
